[V: S1V1] [Q:1/4=100] B B/ B/ G A | B B c A | G B d3/2 c/ | B3 
w: 1.~Lord, while for all man- kind we pray, Of e- very clime and coast, 
w: 2.~Oh, guard our shores from e- very foe, With peace our bor- ders bless, 
w: 3.~U- nite us in the sac- red love Of know- ledge, truth and Thee; 
w: 4.~Here may re- li- gion, pure and mild, Smile on our Sab- bath hours; 
w: 5.~Lord of the na- tions, Thus to Thee Our coun- try we com- mend; 
[V: S1V2]  D D/ ^D/ E F | G =F E D | D G F3/2 F/ | G3 
[V: S2V1]  G, B,/ B,/ B, D | D D C C | B, G, A,3/2 D/ | D3 
