% 13
[V: S1V1]  !sintro! G | e3/2 d/ c B | A B c E | F G B3/2 A/ | G4 !eintro!|]
w: Oh, hear us for our na- tive land, The land we love the most. 
w: With pros- p'rous times our ci- ties crown, Our fields with plen- teous- ness. 
w: And let our hills and val- leys shout The songs of li- ber- ty. 
w: And pi- e- ty and vir- tue bless The home of us and ours. 
w: Be Thou her Re- fuge and her Trust, Her e- ver- las- ting Friend. 
[V: S1V2] D | G3/2 B/ A ^G | A E E E | C B, D3/2 D/ | D4 |]
